      "writtenOn": "2026-10-22T21:00:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would just remove this. As an external user, I would prefer to just get the current clock time rather than (from its perspective) an arbitrary increment of a past clock just to keep a equivalent of a monotonically incrementing timestmap.\n\nIf the wall clock jumped, there is no recoverable thing here. Either they get a fake-non-usable timestamp (Like in this case PAST+N) or CURRENT\u003cPAST. At least in the latter, if I am consuming the timestamp, I can drop that sample and wait for the next (if I am calculating period).",
      "parentUuid": "67904ed9_72a827c1",
      "revId": "b90180b4e6ed4597a4fa1db60b69ebde00dee482",
